    "Fixed graph sparsity priors, strong coefficient shrinkage, g-priors, scale integration, and predictive family scoring do not provide reliable improvement.",
    "S7 localized the promising nonlocal prior's harms to policy feedback rather than terminal inference.",
    "S8 prospectively confirmed dual-posterior separation: baseline posterior for planning plus frozen nonlocal posterior for structural output improved confirmation edge error by 0.470 on average, 95% bootstrap improvement interval [0.316,0.637], with 22/24 wins, zero large harms, improved mean Brier, and identical actions to control.",
    "S9 confirmed transfer of the S8 architecture under weaker Uniform(0.15,0.90) nonzero effects without retuning: mean edge improvement 0.486, 95% bootstrap interval [0.274,0.714], 21/24 wins, one large harm, and acceptable Brier.",
